# Coding & Architecture (always)

## Principles
- Production-ready: Clean Code, SOLID, DRY, KISS, Separation of Concerns.
- One responsibility per class/file/function. Prefer composition over inheritance.
- No unnecessary abstractions. No duplicated business logic.
- Smallest safe change; no unrelated edits.

## Before creating anything
1. Inspect existing structure, similar features, services, helpers, Blade partials, CSS tokens.
2. Reuse or extend what exists; only add a new file if it has a clear single purpose.
3. Follow existing naming (Laravel/PHP + this repo’s folders). Do not invent `helpers/`, `misc/`, `stuff/`.

## Before modifying
- Who imports this? Shared? Tests? Public API?
- Preserve behavior unless the task requires a change.

## Placement (this repo)
- HTTP: `app/Http/Controllers/...` — thin; no heavy business rules.
- Domain/ops: `app/Services/`, `app/Support/`, Actions when the repo already uses them.
- Views: `resources/views/...` — presentation; call services/controllers for logic.
- Public CX: follow `hesetak-platform` + `hesetak-public-pages` skills and `docs/hesetak/`.
- Styles: reuse `mc-*` / existing CSS; no new CSS framework without approval.

## Functions & naming
- Descriptive names (`calculateInvoiceTotal`, not `doThing` / `data` / `temp`).
- Early returns; avoid deep nesting.
- One job per function; extract when hard to read.

## Errors & security
- Never swallow errors. Separate user-facing vs log/debug messages.
- No secrets in code; use `.env`. Validate input server-side.

## Definition of Done
- [ ] Fits architecture; reused existing code where possible
- [ ] No duplicate business logic; clear naming
- [ ] No secrets; intentional error handling
- [ ] No unrelated files/changes
- [ ] Smoke or tests only if actually run — never claim pass without running
